      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this gets stuck retrying when no battery is present, I think we need a little extra state to keep track of how many attempts we\u0027ve made and fail-fast if the battery isn\u0027t working.\n\n```\n    static uint8_t attempt_count \u003d 0;\n    int ret;\n\n    do {\n        ret \u003d i2c_read16(I2C_PORT_BATTERY, addr_flags, cmd, param);\n        if (ret \u003d\u003d EC_SUCCESS) {\n            attempt_count \u003d 0;\n            break;\n        }\n        if (attempt_count \u003c CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART_I2C_RETRY_COUNT) {\n            CPRINTS(\"read failed, wait 50ms then retry (attempt %d)\", i);\n            crec_msleep(50);\n        }\n        attempt_count \u003d MIN(attempt_count + 1, CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART_I2C_RETRY_COUNT);\n    } while (attempt_count \u003c CONFIG_BATTERY_SMART_I2C_RETRY_COUNT);\n    return ret;\n```",
